blocks.text:
Strength ladder:
1. unsupported assertion;
2. personal example;
3. relevant descriptive information;
4. stronger evidence from a credible source/method appropriate to the claim.

> **SIMULATED TRAINING SOURCE — not real research.** A company survey of 480 employees found that most respondents preferred two or three remote days per week, but the survey did not measure productivity.

What can it support? **preference** · What can it not establish? **productivity effect** · Why? **not measured**

tasks.prompt:
Post a 120–160 word position in a moderated discussion. Then reply to one opposing post by:
1. accurately summarising one point before challenging it;
2. adding one source-supported reason or example;
3. using at least one qualification;
4. avoiding strawman language.
